#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": \"Special event\" is ticked on an open-entry product, which cannot "
"block the evening. Untick the field."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": \"Special event\" is ticked on a translation instead of the source "
"product. The plugin reads the marker from the source, so this event will not "
"block the evening. Tick it on the source-language product."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": event capacity is set on a translation instead of the source "
"product. The plugin reads capacity from the source, so the seat limit will "
"not apply. Set the capacity on the source-language product."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": the event is not bound to the shared resource, so it will not appear "
"in the grid."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": the event has no price set (base, block, resource and person-type "
"costs are all 0)."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: product name, 2: event capacity, 3: resource capacity
#, php-format
msgid "\"%1$s\": event capacity (%2$d) exceeds resource capacity (%3$d)."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": the event has no bookable availability rule, so it will not block "
"regular sessions or open entry in its slot."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": the product has no bookable availability rule, so it will not appear "
"in the grid."
msgstr ""

msgid "WooBookings Custom, misconfigured event:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"fix the products below, otherwise they will not behave correctly in the grid:"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: session product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": the session has no bookable availability rule, so the exclusivity "
"that replaces open entry has nothing to derive from. Open entry stays "
"bookable during the session."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: session product name, 2: session rule from, 3: session rule to, 4: open product name, 5: open rule from, 6: open rule to
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%1$s\": the session rule (%2$s to %3$s) covers the entire open-entry "
"window of \"%4$s\" (%5$s to %6$s). Open entry is suppressed completely and "
"nobody can book it."
msgstr ""

msgid "WooBookings Custom, session exclusivity:"
msgstr ""

msgid "check the availability rules of the products below:"
msgstr ""

msgid "WooBookings Custom, product configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "these settings produce a wrong price or block booking:"
msgstr ""

msgid "check these settings:"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": \"Has person types\" is on but \"Has persons\" is off, so the cart "
"ignores person types and prices the booking without them. Turn on \"Has "
"persons\" or turn off person types."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": person types are on but the product has no type, so customers cannot "
"book it. Add person types or turn the field off."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: product name, 2: person type name
#, php-format
msgid "\"%1$s\": person type \"%2$s\" has a price of 0."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": the price is charged twice. Person types have their own prices, and "
"the product also has a base, block or resource cost or Costs table rules, "
"multiplied by the number of people. With prices on person types, set the "
"product costs to 0."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": the shop shows a price of 0 although person types have prices. Save "
"the product again so WooCommerce recalculates the displayed price."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: product name
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%s\": host exceptions are saved on a translation instead of the source "
"product, so the grid will not see them. Set them on the source-language "
"product."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: product name, 2: number of exceptions
#, php-format
msgid ""
"\"%1$s\": %2$d host exception(s) the site will not show (a time outside the "
"schedule or an unavailable person). On those days the weekly host is shown; "
"fix or remove the exception."
msgstr ""

